00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:19.460
hi it's Michelle from lab muffin beauty
science chemistry PhD skincare nerd and

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:24.560
pimple magnet. Acne patches: what are they
and how do they work? that's the topic of

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:28.040
today's video we're talking about all
the different types of stickers that you

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:31.130
can stick on your face when you're
having a breakout if you like this sort

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:34.879
of video give it a thumbs up subscribe
to my channel and click the notification

00:00:34.879 --> 00:00:38.000
bell so you don't miss any of my videos
there are three main types of acne

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.960
patches as of now I'm sure they'll invent
more soon they are hydrocolloid patches

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:46.129
acne treatment patches and microneedle
patches all three of them will help

00:00:46.129 --> 00:00:49.640
protect your pimples from rubbing and
scratching and keep them clean sometimes

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:52.699
if you have a pimple you'll
subconsciously pick at it even in your

00:00:52.699 --> 00:00:56.150
sleep and it protects it from things
like rubbing on your pillowcase or on

00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:59.780
your hair they also help keep an open
wound moist for faster and better

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:03.290
healing depending on the type of patch
they can also help deliver active

00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:07.220
ingredients to your pimple or help
active ingredients absorb better they

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:10.880
can also absorb and draw out any fluid
that's oozing out from your pimple

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:14.780
pimple patches also help protect your
pimples from UV light this is good

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:18.560
because then it reduces the amount of
post inflammatory hyperpigmentation that

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:22.250
can develop these are brown patches on
your skin of pigment that develop after

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:27.080
you've had acne and these can take ages
and ages to fade I have a video all

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:31.220
about how to fade these patches but it's
always best to try to reduce how much

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:35.300
forms in the first place pimple patches
are also usually waterproof so it means

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:38.990
that you don't have to reapply them
every time you wash your face unless you

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:42.740
wash it a bit too hard and water gets
under the bandage let's talk about the

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:47.120
specifics of each of these three types
let's start with hydrocolloid bandages

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:50.810
hydrocolloid bandages were originally
used for ulcers but they became popular

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:54.590
for treating acne in Asia they're
getting a lot easy to find outside of

00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:58.490
Asia as well these bandages are flexible
and they're made of a water attracting

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:02.600
material on a thin plastic membrane
there's adhesive on the other side of

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:05.840
the water attracting material so you
stick it onto your skin with the water

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:09.979
attracting material facing down the
tough plastic outer film is usually made

00:02:09.979 --> 00:02:13.760
of polyurethane and this helps keep
everything in place it's also waterproof

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:17.780
so stops water from evaporating from
your wound and keeps them moist this

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:21.410
helps it heal faster and the new skin
that forms is more supple and flexible

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:25.459
so it doesn't feel tight and stretched
out the plastic film also protects the

00:02:25.459 --> 00:02:28.490
wound against
scratching and it helps stop the water

00:02:28.490 --> 00:02:32.330
attracting material from absorbing water
from the atmosphere you want it to mostly

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:36.260
absorb water from your wound the water
attracting material is usually made of

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:41.540
carboxymethyl cellulose pectin or
gelatin or a combination of these these

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:45.590
materials are really good at attracting
and holding onto water and so it helps

00:02:45.590 --> 00:02:49.250
draw fluid out of your pimple they're
basically just humectant moisturizers

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:53.930
strung together into a giant solid chunk
of humectant as fluid goes into the

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:57.410
bandage it turns into an opaque white
color and so you get this very

00:02:57.410 --> 00:03:01.400
satisfying white spot what's good about
hydrocolloid bandages

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:05.090
there are actually quite a few studies
on the benefits of hydrocolloid bandages

00:03:05.090 --> 00:03:09.620
on open wounds but there's only one on
acne they found out putting 3m acne

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:14.390
dressings on pimples changing them every
two days reduced the severity of acne it

00:03:14.390 --> 00:03:18.200
also reduced redness oiliness and dark
pigmentation and this was compared with

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:21.650
skin tapes sort of like the paper tape
that i used to measure up the size of my

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:25.970
face the downside of hydrocolloid
bandages is that they're a little bit

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:29.630
pricier than other acne treatment
patches they also tend to be thicker

00:03:29.630 --> 00:03:33.500
than acne patches and this gets even
thicker when they absorb more liquid a

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:37.880
few tips for using hydrocolloid bandages
you can buy bigger bandages which are

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:42.260
intended for use on wounds and cut them
up into smaller shapes you can use

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:45.920
scissors or you can use a hole punch
there are thinner hydrocolloid bandages

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:50.330
that you can buy that tend to stick on
and stay on a bit better they also blend

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:53.209
in a bit better if you want to wear them
out during the day when you're buying

00:03:53.209 --> 00:03:57.590
hydrocolloid bandages be really careful
they look almost the same as acne

00:03:57.590 --> 00:04:00.620
treatment patches so make sure it
actually says hydrocolloid on the

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:04.250
package I've heard some people say that
hydrocolloid bandages work fine on

00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:08.570
intact pimples for them personally for
me I found that it works better if I've

00:04:08.570 --> 00:04:12.470
lanced the pimple first so I've poked a
little hole in it you can see some tips

00:04:12.470 --> 00:04:16.070
on how to safely squeeze a pimple in
another video that I've done I've linked

00:04:16.070 --> 00:04:20.330
it in the description the second type of
acne patch is the acne treatment patch

00:04:20.330 --> 00:04:24.020
these contain active ingredients that
are delivered to the pimple while it's

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:28.130
on the most common active ingredients in
these are salicylic acid and tea tree

00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:31.280
oil which are both great for pimples
these look a lot like hydrocolloid

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:34.790
bandages basically they're like the
hydrocolloid bandage minus the

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:38.350
hydrocolloid layer plus the acne
ingredients

00:04:38.350 --> 00:04:41.950
they usually end up being a lot cheaper
as well the benefits of these acne

00:04:41.950 --> 00:04:46.240
treatment patches because they're
occluding the skin they help your skin

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:50.020
absorb ingredients better than if it's
open to the air the patch also keeps the

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:52.870
active ingredients right on the spot
where your pimple is so it doesn't get

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:56.200
rubbed off or moved around on your skin
like with the other patches that helps

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:59.620
protect your pimple from rubbing and
scratching it also keeps your pimple

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:03.640
moist so that it heals faster plus it
keeps it clean the disadvantage of acne

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:07.060
treatment patches is that if you haven't
kept the area clean or if you're

00:05:07.060 --> 00:05:10.420
sensitive to any of the active
ingredients in the patch then your

00:05:10.420 --> 00:05:14.620
reaction will be amplified because of
that occlusive covering one time I

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:19.450
stupidly used one on a pimple right
before a wedding and overnight the

00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:24.010
pimple became three times its size so
the moral of the story there is try the

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:28.750
patch before it's an important event a
few tips for using acne treatment

00:05:28.750 --> 00:05:32.620
patches make sure your skin is clean
underneath the patch before you put it

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:35.890
on it will stick on better plus it'll
reduce the chance of you sealing

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:39.370
something irritating onto your skin even
though the active ingredients in the

00:05:39.370 --> 00:05:43.000
patches are usually quite similar they
still perform quite differently so make

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:46.120
sure you've read some reviews before you
try buying some when you're buying it

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:50.380
again they look a lot like hydrocolloid
patches so make sure you check which one

00:05:50.380 --> 00:05:53.770
you're buying acne treatment patches
will usually have the active ingredients

00:05:53.770 --> 00:05:57.280
somewhere in the description plus
they'll be a fair bit cheaper than

00:05:57.280 --> 00:06:02.050
hydrocolloid bandages finally dissolving
microneedle patches these are the newest

00:06:02.050 --> 00:06:05.860
fanciest ones on the market these are
sticky bandages that have a water

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:10.330
soluble chip on top this chip has lots
of little microneedles on it think of

00:06:10.330 --> 00:06:14.620
it like a specially shaped chip of sugar
that's embedded with active ingredients

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:18.730
again the active ingredients in these
are things that you usually find in acne

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:23.380
spot treatments so things like salicylic
acid niacinamide antioxidants and

00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:27.040
hyaluronic acid in some of these the
sticky bandage is also a hydrocolloid

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:31.660
bandage too the key idea with these is
that the microneedles can get beyond

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:35.290
the skin barrier the stratum corneum
this top layer of skin that acts as a

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:39.370
really good barrier to any active
ingredients that you put on the micro

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:43.240
needles get past this so that the active
ingredients can get to the pimple where

00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:48.150
they're needed this is what the micro
needles look like up close

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:52.840
please excuse my shaky camera work it is
a microscope so every time I wiggled

00:06:52.840 --> 00:06:58.479
it shows up like a giant wiggle the
shape and length of the microneedles

00:06:58.479 --> 00:07:04.360
depends on the specific brand and
product that you're using some needles

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:18.340
are round some are square some are even
cross shaped it takes about two hours

00:07:18.340 --> 00:07:22.660
for the microneedles to dissolve in the
water that's naturally already present

00:07:22.660 --> 00:07:31.930
in your skin these microneedles might
look really pointy and scary but these

00:07:31.930 --> 00:07:38.199
are massively zoomed in you can see
relative to my finger they're really

00:07:38.199 --> 00:07:43.150
tiny and they don't go in very deep at
all you might have seen people use

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:47.560
dermarollers and there's lots of blood and
pain involved but the microneedles in

00:07:47.560 --> 00:07:51.669
these patches are a lot shorter and so
they don't reach deep enough to draw out

00:07:51.669 --> 00:07:56.289
any blood or cause any pain in terms of
comfort usually it doesn't really feel

00:07:56.289 --> 00:08:00.400
like much it feels a little bit stiff
and rough until you get used to it and I

00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:04.090
think mostly that's just because you've
got this hard chip stuck to your skin the

00:08:04.090 --> 00:08:07.510
biggest advantage of these microneedle
patches is that they can get through the

00:08:07.510 --> 00:08:10.780
stratum corneum and so they deliver
active ingredients a lot more

00:08:10.780 --> 00:08:14.380
efficiently active ingredients also
last a lot longer in microneedle

00:08:14.380 --> 00:08:19.240
patches than in say a water-based serum
and so things like antioxidants are more

00:08:19.240 --> 00:08:23.020
likely to still be active when you apply
it the biggest disadvantage of these is

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:27.070
that they tend to be really expensive
and that's because there's just a lot

00:08:27.070 --> 00:08:30.849
that goes into making these there's also
a lot of packaging involved with these

00:08:30.849 --> 00:08:34.659
because the microneedles are quite
fragile they need to be protected from

00:08:34.659 --> 00:08:38.560
getting bumped against before you put it
on your skin they also need to be

00:08:38.560 --> 00:08:41.289
protected against moisture in the air
because then they'll just start

00:08:41.289 --> 00:08:44.440
dissolving and so usually if they're
packaged individually or in small

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:48.220
packets with some sort of water
absorbing desiccant a few chips were

00:08:48.220 --> 00:08:52.390
using these again make sure your skin is
clean before you put them on and make

00:08:52.390 --> 00:08:55.420
sure it's also dry so that the micro
needles can actually get through your

00:08:55.420 --> 00:08:58.660
skin before they start dissolving it's
recommended that you use these at the

00:08:58.660 --> 00:09:01.900
very first sign of a pimple I personally
found these most effective

00:09:01.900 --> 00:09:05.770
on medium depth pimples not the
really really deep cystic pimples that

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:09.880
you sometimes get under the skin usually
it's with pimples that come to a head

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:13.930
after a few days when I use these I can
actually see the people stop growing

00:09:13.930 --> 00:09:17.950
after a few hours and it works even
better overnight which one I prefer

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:21.670
really depends on the type of pimple I
have this might be completely different

00:09:21.670 --> 00:09:25.510
for you this is just from my personal
experience if I have a pimple that's got

00:09:25.510 --> 00:09:28.960
lots of fluid or pus then I go for a
hydrocolloid bandage because it's

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:32.920
capable of absorbing all the fluid
without just sliding off if I have a

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:37.180
really nasty medium depth pimple then I
go straight for the microneedle patches

00:09:37.180 --> 00:09:41.500
I usually save these for the nastier
pimples because they are a bit more

00:09:41.500 --> 00:09:44.920
expensive so I try to be a bit more
sparing when I use them I haven't had

00:09:44.920 --> 00:09:48.760
great luck with acne patches but I know
other people have I would personally use

00:09:48.760 --> 00:09:53.140
them on slightly smaller less inflamed
pimples that I feel like don't really

00:09:53.140 --> 00:09:56.710
deserve a microneedle patch I think the
most important thing when you're using

00:09:56.710 --> 00:10:00.550
these is to make sure you clean your
skin really well before you apply it on

00:10:00.550 --> 00:10:04.870
I've listed a few brands of acne patches
that I've tried in the caption I haven't

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:08.590
tried a ton of them so please leave me a
comment if you have any recommendations

